import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 210 | Joint Contracting Mechanism Realm-Wide Adaptation: Realm Differences in Resource Allocation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 210 | Joint Contracting Mechanism Realm-Wide Adaptation: Realm Differences in Resource Allocation","no":210,"tags":["Realm","Joint Contracting","Resource Allocation","More Work More Gain","Realm-Wide Adaptation"],"module":1,"related":["22-Resource Allocation Joint Contracting Mechanism","06-More Work More Gain Distribution Principle","18-Cultivation Resource Opening Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0210_模块1-联产承包机制全境适配-资源分配的境界差异.md","filePath":"en/0210_模块1-联产承包机制全境适配-资源分配的境界差异.md"}'),n={name:"en/0210_模块1-联产承包机制全境适配-资源分配的境界差异.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,u,h){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-210-joint-contracting-mechanism-realm-wide-adaptation-realm-differences-in-resource-allocation" tabindex="-1">Entry 210 | Joint Contracting Mechanism Realm-Wide Adaptation: Realm Differences in Resource Allocation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-210-joint-contracting-mechanism-realm-wide-adaptation-realm-differences-in-resource-allocation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 210 | Joint Contracting Mechanism Realm-Wide Adaptation: Realm Differences in Resource Allocation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 22, 06, 18</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-more-work-more-gain-but-first-guarantee-everyone-has-food" tabindex="-1">Introduction: More work more gain, but first guarantee everyone has food <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-more-work-more-gain-but-first-guarantee-everyone-has-food" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: More work more gain, but first guarantee everyone has food&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The joint contracting mechanism is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s resource allocation base: allocation of cultivation resources by contribution, more work more gain, no work no gain. But &quot;more work more gain&quot; is not a rerun of the jungle law — it has a hard prerequisite: the everyone-has-a-road guarantee system first guarantees every life&#39;s basic cultivation conditions, then on top of this opens gaps by contribution. This entry explains how this mechanism adapts across the nine realms: at different realm segments, how the proportion of basic guarantee vs more-work-more-gain changes.</p><p>The six top-level axioms are the allocation mechanism&#39;s ethical base: the anti-predation axiom stipulates resources come from creating increments not predating stock; the republican axiom of Myriad Races stipulates basic guarantee treats Myriad Races equally; the collective ascension axiom requires high-rank resources to be prioritized for lifting the whole; the causal self-discipline axiom requires allocation throughout leave traces auditable; the law-first axiom stipulates allocation formulas be stable, not changed by personal favor; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-realm-wide-allocation-structure" tabindex="-1">I. Realm-Wide Allocation Structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-realm-wide-allocation-structure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Realm-Wide Allocation Structure&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Realm Segment</th><th>Basic Guarantee (everyone gets a share)</th><th>More Work More Gain (floats by contribution)</th><th>Resource Nature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sense–Condensed</td><td>Vast majority</td><td>Very small</td><td>Free basic methods, public cultivation grounds</td></tr><tr><td>Transform–Law</td><td>Basic + advanced ration</td><td>Larger float</td><td>Advanced resources, mentor qualification</td></tr><tr><td>Dao–Dao Integration</td><td>Basic guarantee</td><td>Large-proportion float</td><td>High-grade resources, anchor access</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary-Breaking–World-Creation</td><td>Basic guarantee</td><td>By post contribution</td><td>Plane-level resource dispatch</td></tr><tr><td>Origin Realm</td><td>Post benefits</td><td>By public responsibility</td><td>Cosmic-level resources, law participation rights</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The pattern is clear: <strong>the lower the rank, the higher the basic guarantee proportion; the higher the rank, the higher the more-work-more-gain and post-benefits proportion.</strong> Low ranks guarantee no one starves; high ranks reward real contribution.</p><h2 id="ii-why-low-ranks-get-universal-benefit-first" tabindex="-1">II. Why Low Ranks Get Universal Benefit First <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-low-ranks-get-universal-benefit-first" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why Low Ranks Get Universal Benefit First&quot;">​</a></h2><p>At Sense–Condensed, cultivators are still laying foundations; if &quot;more work more gain&quot; were cruelly applied then, it would repeat old systems&#39; tragedy of &quot;bottom ranks cannot afford cultivation.&quot; Thus symbiotic civilization sets basic resources — methods, cultivation grounds, initial multiplication devices — as free public goods, letting anyone start the road first. This is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; landing in allocation.</p><h2 id="iii-why-high-ranks-are-by-contribution-and-post" tabindex="-1">III. Why High Ranks Are by Contribution and Post <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-why-high-ranks-are-by-contribution-and-post" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Why High Ranks Are by Contribution and Post&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Above Dao Origin, cultivators have already proven their potential; at this point resource allocation should tilt toward those &quot;contributing more to the whole network&quot;: only contribution values in the top 20% qualify to compete for high-grade resources; Origin Realm&#39;s resource benefits are tied to their public post (Entry 207). This both rewards contribution and directs resources to where value can be amplified most.</p><h2 id="iv-anti-monopoly-and-anti-egalitarianism" tabindex="-1">IV. Anti-Monopoly and Anti-Egalitarianism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-anti-monopoly-and-anti-egalitarianism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Anti-Monopoly and Anti-Egalitarianism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Joint contracting must simultaneously guard against two extremes:</p><ul><li><strong>Anti-monopoly</strong>: the law forbids anyone monopolizing resource allocation rights; high-grade resources although allocated by contribution, their total expands with civilizational increments, no zero-sum cake-cutting;</li><li><strong>Anti-egalitarianism</strong>: anti-predation is not communal pot luck, contribution differences really exist, more work more gain retains reasonable gaps.</li></ul><p>Document 06 is clear: symbiotic civilization recognizes differences in evolutionary results, but differences must come from one&#39;s own effort and contribution, not violence and birth.</p><h2 id="v-relationship-with-anti-predation" tabindex="-1">V. Relationship with Anti-Predation <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-relationship-with-anti-predation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Relationship with Anti-Predation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Joint contracting is anti-predation&#39;s economic alternative: old systems allocate resources by &quot;robbing&quot;; symbiotic civilization allocates resources by &quot;making&quot; — the larger the increment you create, the more you receive. Thus the strong one&#39;s rise is no longer at the weak one&#39;s predated expense, and the entire resource pool grows larger.</p><h2 id="vi-transitional-protection-during-transition" tabindex="-1">VI. Transitional Protection During Transition <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-transitional-protection-during-transition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Transitional Protection During Transition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Transitioning from predatory allocation to joint contracting, the hardest part is not designing formulas, but bearing the bottom cultivators exploited by old systems for a millennium. Symbiotic civilization sets transition protection for this: in early transition, Sense–Condensed stages have no contribution threshold, purely universal rationing; for cultivators converted from the Predatory Faction, their conversion-period contribution is counted as &quot;correction is contribution,&quot; not requiring them to match native symbionts&#39; output from day one. This transitional design avoids secondary harm of &quot;the new system eliminates old victims from day one,&quot; letting joint contracting both open reasonable gaps yet not replay the jungle during transition.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: resources directed to those contributing most, avoiding waste of &quot;lying on resources idling&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: allocation by contribution not robbery, economically eliminating predation motive</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style resources rely on sects and holy grace, commoners get none; in Heng Yuan Zhou basics are free and high ranks by contribution, a poor family can rise through hard work</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: basic guarantee treats all Myriad Races groups equally, contribution measurement recognizes each race&#39;s characteristic contributions</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: allocation formulas, contribution measurement, and anti-monopoly clauses are all public</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The essence of joint contracting realm-wide adaptation is one sentence: low ranks let everyone have a road, high ranks let more work more gain. Land this sentence on every segment of the nine realms, and Heng Yuan Zhou is neither communal-pot egalitarianism nor weak-eats-strong hunting ground — it is an allocation machine that grows the cake bigger.</p><p>In the final analysis, joint contracting mechanism realm-wide adaptation · realm differences in resource allocation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Resource Allocation Joint Contracting Mechanism</a> · <a href="./06-多劳多得分配原理.html">06-More Work More Gain Distribution Principle</a> · <a href="./18-修炼资源开放机制.html">18-Cultivation Resource Opening Mechanism</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const g=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
